# reprepro distributions config for the DuckDB packaging fork's
# GitHub-Pages-hosted apt repository.
#
# One stanza per (suite, codename) pair we ship.  Each suite gets
# its own dists/<codename>/Release that reprepro signs; users put
# the matching codename in their /etc/apt/sources.list.d entry.
#
# SignWith: yes
#   Tells reprepro to sign with gpg's default-key setting (set in
#   ~/.gnupg/gpg.conf or via gpg --default-key on invocation).
#   Maintainers who want to be explicit can override by exporting
#   GNUPGHOME or passing --default-key to publish-apt-pages.sh.
#   The signing key fingerprint is NOT stored in this repo --
#   maintainers must export the key locally before running the
#   publish script.  See debian/README.apt-pages "First-time setup".
#
# Architectures: amd64 + arm64 only.  riscv64 is built under
# emulation (continue-on-error in CI) and is NOT promoted to the
# apt repo until we have a real consumer with riscv64 hardware
# asking for it -- otherwise we'd ship .debs without an effective
# way for a maintainer to test installs.
#
# When adding a new suite, also extend publish-apt-pages.sh's
# DEB_SUITES variable.

Origin: mgajda/duckdb-deb
Label: DuckDB (mgajda packaging fork)
Suite: trixie
Codename: trixie
Architectures: amd64 arm64 source
Components: main
Description: DuckDB binaries built for Debian trixie
SignWith: yes

